  my C4), the left corner can't grow upward. Prefer C4 + G6 (G12 draw) or C4 + G7: groups
  on DIFFERENT sides, so no single black wall can sandwich both.
- After the wedge, answer at once on the bottom edge (D2/F2) so the wall can't reach row 2;
  B E2 then D2/G2 hanes cut both my corners down.
- Never extend a group into a long wall between black stones (D6/D5) while its eye space is
  still open. Make eye shape first: in the corner, the 1-2 point (B1/B2) is vital. Black B1
  gave A1/B1/B2 = one eye.
- Don't start a second weak group (E7 top invasion) while my bottom groups are unsettled.

